            <ArticleTitle>Balloon entrapment in a coronary artery: potential serious complications of balloon rupture.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>23-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of balloon catheter rupture with subsequent entrapment during percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty. The presence of a calcified, distal lesion is believed to have prevented withdrawal of the broken catheter. A nonsurgical retrieval technique, using a second dilation system, was used to free the catheter.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
